   436	# =============================================================================
   437	# PLAN-167 — _ownership_verdict: THE ownership decision.
   438	#
   439	# install.sh and upgrade.sh stop deciding and start executing. Every defect in
   440	# the 35-finding S296 review series was a cell of this space whose answer was
   441	# decided branch-locally, so two branches could disagree about the same
   442	# question and nothing detected it.
   443	#
   444	#   $1 surface        spec | protocol | marker
   445	#   $2 prior_record   none | hash | link_match | link_retargeted
   446	#   $3 live_type      absent | dir | dir_empty | regular | symlink | special
   447	#                     | ancestor_symlink
   448	#   $4 live_content   pristine | legacy_pristine | legacy_pristine_partial
   449	#                     | edited | -
   450	#   $5 source_has     yes | no
   451	#   $6 mode           copy | link
   452	#   $7 ceremony       user | maintainer
   453	#   $8 operation      install_fresh | install_rerun | upgrade
   454	#   $9 skip_requested none | self | descendant
   455	#
   456	#   stdout: "<VERDICT> <HASH_SOURCE>", rc 0
   457	#   rc 1, no output: a combination the legality rules forbid.
   458	#
   459	# PURE: no filesystem, no globals, no environment. Callers observe the nine
   460	# dimensions and pass them in. That purity is what lets the same table drive a
   461	# millisecond unit oracle as well as the ~25-minute end-to-end suite; S296 had
   462	# only the slow instrument, at one cell per ~40-minute round.
   463	#
   464	# ABORT_SURFACE is deliberately NOT produced here (round-1 consensus C2). A
   465	# failed backup is not a property of these nine dimensions — it is the CALLER
   466	# failing to carry out a verdict it was handed. And per INV-3 that failure
   467	# NEVER advances the record: recording a delivery that did not happen is the
   468	# over-claiming direction ADR-155-AMEND-1 §3 forbids.
   469	#
   470	# Contract: docs/ownership-decision-table.md · Truth: scripts/tests/ownership_table.tsv
   471	# =============================================================================
   472	_ownership_verdict() {
   473	  _ov_surface="$1"; _ov_prior="$2";  _ov_ltype="$3"; _ov_lcontent="$4"
   474	  _ov_shas="$5";    _ov_mode="$6";   _ov_cer="$7";   _ov_op="$8"; _ov_skip="$9"
   475	
   476	  # Do not touch the surface; decide the RECORD. Ownership continuity and the
   477	  # digit it carries are separate decisions, and moving one without the other
   478	  # produced four distinct defects — so they are resolved together, once.
   479	  _ov_carry() {
   480	    case "$_ov_prior" in
   481	      link_match)      printf 'PRESERVE_OWNED LINK_RECORD';  return 0 ;;
   482	      link_retargeted) printf 'PRESERVE_UNOWNED HASH_NONE'; return 0 ;;
   483	      none)            printf 'PRESERVE_UNOWNED HASH_NONE';  return 0 ;;
   484	    esac
   485	    # prior_record=hash. HASH_TARGET is never an option: it re-baselines the
   486	    # bytes now on disk, which is how a later upgrade comes to overwrite an
   487	    # adopter edit and uninstall comes to delete it.
   488	    if [ "$_ov_surface" = "protocol" ] \
   489	       || [ "$_ov_shas" = "no" ] \
   490	       || [ "$_ov_ltype" = "dir_empty" ]; then
   491	      printf 'PRESERVE_OWNED HASH_PRIOR_RECORD'   # no source bytes to hash
   492	    else
   493	      printf 'PRESERVE_OWNED HASH_SOURCE'
   494	    fi
   495	  }
   496	
   497	  # The framework must not claim this path. Whether a record existed changes
   498	  # only which NAME the observation takes (OQ-9 — the evidence that these are
   499	  # one outcome, not two).
   500	  # OQ-9 (ratificada pelo Owner 2026-08-07): PRESERVE_UNOWNED é o único nome.
   501	  # OMIT_RECORD dizia a mesma coisa — sem registro no disco — e diferia apenas
   502	  # por já existir registro antes, que é a coluna prior_record. Um membro de
   503	  # enum redundante é onde dois ramos discordam sobre qual deles se aplica.
   504	  _ov_unowned() { printf 'PRESERVE_UNOWNED HASH_NONE'; }
   505	
   506	  # --- Stage A: gates that refuse to act, in priority order ------------------
   507	
   508	  # A1. The source cannot deliver this surface.
   509	  if [ "$_ov_shas" = "no" ]; then
   510	    case "$_ov_surface" in
   511	      marker)   printf 'PRESERVE_UNOWNED HASH_NONE'; return 0 ;;  # --pin: readers fall back to VERSION
   512	      protocol) return 1 ;;                                  # R-03: generated, never absent
   513	      *)        _ov_carry; return 0 ;;
   514	    esac
   515	  fi
   516	
   517	  # A2. A user ceremony never receives the root surfaces (WS4).
   518	  if [ "$_ov_cer" = "user" ] && [ "$_ov_surface" != "marker" ]; then
   519	    if [ "$_ov_op" = "install_fresh" ]; then printf 'PRESERVE_UNOWNED HASH_NONE'
   520	    else _ov_carry; fi
   521	    return 0
   522	  fi
   523	
   524	  # A3. Reachable only by writing THROUGH a symlink, out of the target tree.
   525	  # Always unowned: the relpath sanitizer already dropped any record whose path
   526	  # crosses a symlink, so there is no record left to carry (docs §5.8).
   527	  if [ "$_ov_ltype" = "ancestor_symlink" ]; then _ov_unowned; return 0; fi
   528	
   529	  # A4. A leaf symlink is healthy ONLY as the recorded link-mode delivery.
   530	  # The absence of a LINK row is not a match — it is the absence of evidence.
   531	  if [ "$_ov_ltype" = "symlink" ]; then
   532	    if [ "$_ov_prior" = "link_match" ]; then printf 'PRESERVE_OWNED LINK_RECORD'
   533	    else _ov_unowned; fi
   534	    return 0
   535	  fi
   536	
   537	  # A5. Anything that exists but is not shaped like this surface is
   538	  # adopter-owned: never write into it, never through it, never block on it.
   539	  case "$_ov_surface" in
   540	    spec)
   541	      case "$_ov_ltype" in special) _ov_unowned; return 0 ;; esac ;;
   542	    protocol|marker)
   543	      case "$_ov_ltype" in dir|dir_empty|special) _ov_unowned; return 0 ;; esac ;;
   544	  esac
   545	
   546	  # A6. An explicit skip is honoured as a UNIT — a partial contract refresh is
   547	  # incoherent, so a descendant skip preserves the whole tree.
   548	  if [ "$_ov_skip" != "none" ]; then _ov_carry; return 0; fi
   549	
   550	  # --- Stage B: ownership resolution ----------------------------------------
   551	  _ov_owned=""
   552	  if [ "$_ov_prior" = "hash" ] || [ "$_ov_prior" = "link_match" ]; then
   553	    _ov_owned=1
   554	  elif [ "$_ov_ltype" = "absent" ]; then
   555	    _ov_owned=1                                   # new delivery
   556	  elif [ "$_ov_lcontent" = "pristine" ] || [ "$_ov_lcontent" = "legacy_pristine" ]; then
   557	    _ov_owned=1                                   # current-source takeover / legacy migration
   558	  elif [ "$_ov_lcontent" = "degraded" ]; then
   559	    # PLAN-168 W2 (AC-6b, Owner decision D2): a DEGRADED body — byte-exact
   560	    # reconstruction of the {{PROTOCOL_SOURCE}}-literal template the broken
   561	    # upgrade wrote (recognized by _protocol_pointer_is_degraded, NEVER by
   562	    # substring) — is the framework's own output, not adopter content. Owned
   563	    # even without a delivery record, same content-proven takeover doctrine
   564	    # as legacy_pristine (the r20 precedent). Downstream this falls into the
   565	    # protocol REFRESH route: the cure, with the standard backup.
   566	    _ov_owned=1
   567	  fi
   568	  # legacy_pristine_partial is deliberately NOT owned: every regular file may
   569	  # match a shipped release, but a tree carrying an entry the fingerprint
   570	  # cannot inventory has not been inventoried, and a partial inventory must
   571	  # never certify a wholesale replace (ADR-155-AMEND-1 §4).
   572	
   573	  if [ -z "$_ov_owned" ]; then _ov_unowned; return 0; fi
   574	
   575	  # --- Stage C: execution ---------------------------------------------------
   576	  if [ "$_ov_ltype" = "absent" ]; then
   577	    case "$_ov_surface" in
   578	      protocol) printf 'DELIVER HASH_CANONICAL_POINTER' ;;
   579	      *)        printf 'DELIVER HASH_SOURCE' ;;
   580	    esac
   581	    return 0
   582	  fi
   583	
   584	  # An install rerun does not re-deliver an existing surface; it decides the
   585	  # record. Only the upgrade's forced route replaces content.
   586	  if [ "$_ov_op" != "upgrade" ]; then _ov_carry; return 0; fi
   587	
   588	  # The pointer is the ONE surface where an adopter edit is PRESERVED rather
   589	  # than treated as a fork. SPEC/v1 is deliberately the opposite: it is the
   590	  # published compliance CONTRACT, so an edit is a fork and the forced route
   591	  # replaces it (ADR-155-AMEND-1 §4). The root PROTOCOL.md is adopter-editable
   592	  # prose, and overwriting a customised one is the verified S238 data loss that
   593	  # ADR-155 decision (iii) exists to close.
   594	  #
   595	  # The recorded digest stays CANONICAL either way: recording the customised
   596	  # bytes would make the NEXT upgrade read H_dst==H_base and clobber them.
   597	  if [ "$_ov_surface" = "protocol" ] && [ "$_ov_lcontent" = "edited" ]; then
   598	    printf 'PRESERVE_OWNED HASH_CANONICAL_POINTER'
   599	    return 0
   600	  fi
   601	
   602	  case "$_ov_surface" in
   603	    protocol) printf 'REFRESH HASH_CANONICAL_POINTER' ;;
   604	    *)        printf 'REFRESH HASH_SOURCE' ;;
   605	  esac
   606	}
   607	# =============================================================================
   608	# PLAN-168 W2 (AC-6, Owner decision D1-b) — the ONE protocol-pointer generator.
   609	#
   610	# INV-4 existed because install.sh and upgrade.sh each carried a private copy
   611	# of the pointer heredoc: install substituted {{PROTOCOL_SOURCE}} in a later
   612	# pass, upgrade hashed (and on REFRESH wrote) the body with the token still
   613	# literal. Two bodies for the same file. This library is the cure for the
   614	# CLASS: both callers render through the same function, so the bodies cannot
   615	# diverge again (ADR-155 decision (i), applied to CONTENT — the shared
   616	# enumeration solved WHICH paths both sides touch; this solves WHAT they
   617	# produce).
   618	#
   619	# Sourced by scripts/install.sh and scripts/upgrade.sh (same $SCRIPT_DIR
   620	# pattern as _hash_lib.sh). Bash 3.2-compatible, stdlib/POSIX-tools only.
   621	#
   622	# Functions:
   623	#   _render_protocol_pointer SOURCE_DIR TARGET PROFILE STACK PROTOCOL_SOURCE
   624	#       Emit the COMPLETE healthy file content ("# Protocol reference" header
   625	#       included, trailing newline included). Inside-target checkouts get the
   626	#       relative form; everything else gets the PROTOCOL_SOURCE-resolved form
   627	#       (never the literal token — the caller passes the resolved value).
   628	#   _render_protocol_pointer_degraded TARGET PROFILE STACK
   629	#       Emit the DEGRADED file content: the outside-target template with
   630	#       {{PROTOCOL_SOURCE}} kept literal. This is byte-for-byte what the
    35	> the table agree with each other. Reconciling either one is W2 work, after
    36	> ratification.
    37	
    38	## 1. What this document is, and why it exists
    39	
    40	`ADR-155-AMEND-1` decided that framework ownership of the three
    41	**conditional** surfaces — root `PROTOCOL.md`, the `SPEC/v1` contract tree,
    42	and the `.claude/.framework-version` marker — derives from the **registered
    43	delivery record**, never from the ceremony alone and never from file
    44	presence.
    45	
    46	The decision was right. Its *realization* was a cascade of `if` branches
    47	spread across `scripts/install.sh`, `scripts/upgrade.sh` and
    48	`scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh`. That shape has a measured failure
    49	mode: over eleven consecutive cross-model review rounds on the same code,
    50	**35 distinct defects** were reported, and roughly half of the later ones
    51	were regressions introduced by the fix for the round immediately before.
    52	The 45-check end-to-end suite stayed green throughout — it exercises eight
    53	scenarios, and the decision space is a nine-dimensional product.
    54	
    55	The cause is not carelessness. It is that **"correct" was being decided one
    56	branch at a time**, so two branches could encode contradictory answers to
    57	the same question and nothing would notice. This document makes the space
    58	explicit so that contradictions surface *before* they become defects.
    59	
    60	Division of labour, strictly observed:
    61	
    62	| Artifact | Role |
    63	|---|---|
    64	| this document | defines the dimensions, the legality rules, and the reasoning |
    65	| `scripts/tests/ownership_table.tsv` | **the truth** — one row per legal cell, with its expected verdict |
    66	| `scripts/tests/test-ownership-table.sh` | executes every row against the **real** scripts |
    67	
    68	**No value is duplicated between this document and the TSV.** If you want to
    69	know what a given cell decides, read the TSV. If you want to know *why the
    70	cell exists at all*, read this.
    71	
    72	## 2. The nine dimensions
    73	
    74	A "cell" is one assignment of all nine. The subject under test is one
    75	surface's outcome on one run.
    76	
    77	### 2.1 `surface`
    78	
    79	| Value | Path | Shape |
    80	|---|---|---|
    81	| `spec` | `SPEC/v1` | a **tree** |
    82	| `protocol` | root `PROTOCOL.md` | a **generated pointer** — no source file; the body is a heredoc built from `$SOURCE_DIR`/`$TARGET`/`$PROFILE`/`$STACK` |
    83	| `marker` | `.claude/.framework-version` | a tracked single-line file |
    84	
    85	The three differ in more than their path, and every difference has produced
    86	at least one defect. `spec` is the only tree (so it is the only surface with
    87	descendants, per-file records, and a "partially populated" state);
    88	`protocol` is the only surface with no bytes in the source (so `source_has`
    89	is meaningless for it, and its baseline digest comes from a *computed*
    90	canonical hash); `marker` is the only surface inside `.claude/`, so it is
    91	the only one both ceremonies receive.
    92	
    93	### 2.2 `prior_record` — what the PRE-run baseline manifest says
    94	
    95	| Value | Meaning |
    96	|---|---|
    97	| `none` | no record line for this relpath |
    98	| `hash` | a `<64-hex>  <relpath>` record |
    99	| `link_match` | a `LINK  <relpath>  <target>` record whose target equals the live `readlink` |
   100	| `link_retargeted` | a `LINK` record whose target does **not** equal the live `readlink` |
   101	
   102	This dimension describes the **previous** run's testimony, read before
   103	anything is written this run. It is the operative meaning of "registered
   104	delivery" in ADR-155-AMEND-1 §3.
   105	
   106	### 2.3 `live_type` — `lstat` of the destination, never following
   107	
   108	`absent` · `dir` · `dir_empty` · `regular` · `symlink` · `special`
   109	(FIFO, socket, device) · `ancestor_symlink`.
   110	
   111	`ancestor_symlink` is a value of this dimension rather than a tenth
   112	dimension because the decision function short-circuits on it *before* it
   113	ever looks at the leaf — exactly as it does for `special`. It answers the
   114	same question ("what kind of destination is this?") with "one reachable only
   115	by writing through a symlink out of the target tree".
   430	
   431	The table had nine `protocol` rows and none for the combination that matters
   432	most: an **adopter-customised pointer on a normal (maintainer) upgrade**.
   433	`OWN-0072` covers the same content under `ceremony=user`; the ordinary path
   434	was simply absent.
   435	
   436	Deriving its expected pair exposed a **data-loss defect in the proposed
   437	decision function**. For that cell the function returned `REFRESH` — it would
   438	have overwritten a customised root `PROTOCOL.md`. That is the verified S238
   439	loss that ADR-155 decision (iii) exists to close, and the live code has
   440	preserved it correctly all along.
   441	
   442	The asymmetry the function was missing is deliberate and is now stated in it:
   443	
   444	| Surface | An adopter edit is… | Because |
   445	|---|---|---|
   446	| `SPEC/v1` | a **fork of the contract** → forced refresh | it is the published compliance contract (ADR-155-AMEND-1 §4) |
   447	| `PROTOCOL.md` | **adopter content** → preserved | overwriting it is the verified S238 loss (ADR-155 (iii)) |
   448	
   449	Both record a **canonical** digest regardless, because recording the
   450	customised bytes would make the *next* upgrade read `H_dst == H_base` and
   451	clobber them — the C.5 idempotency trap.
   452	
   453	Two things are worth separating here. The defect was in the **new** code, not
   454	the old: a refactor that had been driven only by "keep the map green" would
   455	have shipped it, because **no existing row covered the cell**. What found it
   456	was asking the completeness question — *which combinations does this surface
   457	have, and is each one present?* — which is the one question a per-branch
   458	review never asks.
   459	
   460	### 5.4e Install and upgrade generate DIFFERENT pointers — every upgrade breaks it (CLOSED by PLAN-168 W2 — INV-4; discovery record below)
   461	
   462	Chasing a `HASH_UNCLASSIFIED` observation led to a defect in the live code
   463	that has nothing to do with ownership records.
   464	
   465	`install.sh` writes the root pointer and then **substitutes** its
   466	placeholders, so the adopter gets a real path. `upgrade.sh` regenerates the
   467	same file from a heredoc that leaves `{{PROTOCOL_SOURCE}}` **literal**, and
   468	nothing substitutes it afterwards. Verified against the live tree:
   469	
   470	| after | literal `{{PROTOCOL_SOURCE}}` occurrences |
   660	  Dropping the marker record makes readers fall back to a `VERSION` the
   661	  upgrade never writes on an external target. A truthful signal requires
   662	  deriving from the pinned source; that is a new mechanism, not a cell.
   663	
   664	- **OQ-4 — Splitting `FMS_PROTOCOL_HASH`.** It carries
   665	  `HASH_CANONICAL_POINTER` on one path and `HASH_PRIOR_RECORD` on another.
   666	  Splitting is the model-faithful move; it also changes a canonical-guarded
   667	  signature.
   668	
   669	- **OQ-5 — Where does `_ownership_verdict()` live?**
   670	  A new library file is a new canonical path, which requires a
   671	  `_CANONICAL_GUARDS` entry and therefore a kernel ceremony. PLAN-167 §4
   672	  states a preference for the already-guarded
   673	  `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh` absent a reasoned veto. A veto
   674	  escalates to the Owner — it does not become an overnight kernel ceremony.
   675	
   676	- **OQ-6 — Does `install_rerun` need `--skip`?** R-02 prunes the whole
   677	  column for install today. If the answer is "install should honour skips
   678	  too", that is a feature decision, and the pruned cells become legal.
   679	
   680	- **OQ-7 — RESOLVED in round 1.** `fault` is now a real column (§2.10) and
   681	  `legacy_pristine_partial` a real `live_content` value. Both were prose
   682	  directives; both are now dimensions. The text below is kept as the record
   683	  of the question.
   684	
   685	  ~~**`fault` is a tenth axis the column contract does not have.**~~
   686	  Three defects are reachable only under an injected environmental failure
   687	  (an unwritable backup directory). That is not a property of the target, so
   688	  it is not `live_type`; it is a genuine tenth dimension. PLAN-167 §W0.2
   689	  froze the TSV at fourteen columns, so it currently rides in `note` as
   690	  `fault=<enum>`. This is **declared, not smuggled**: the debate should
   691	  either bless a fifteenth column or rule those rows out of scope. Leaving
   692	  it in free text is the one option that should not survive — a dimension
   693	  the harness parses out of prose is a dimension nothing validates.
   694	
   695	- **OQ-9 — Is `OMIT_RECORD` an independent verdict at all?**
   696	  *New evidence from the shadow run:* the `OWN-0030` divergence exists ONLY
   697	  because the two instruments answer different questions — the suite asks
   698	  "did a record disappear?" and the function asks "was there a trustworthy
   699	  prior record?". Both end with no record on disk. **If the two verdicts
   700	  collapse into one, that divergence stops existing**, which is a second,
   701	  independent argument for the collapse: a distinction that generates
   702	  disagreement while having no observable consequence is not carrying its
   703	  weight.
   704	  Filling the table, every `OMIT_RECORD` row turned out to be a row that would
