   107	### §0.3 — `release.yml` 24h RC hold enforcement
   108	
   109	Debate Round 1 consensus §S3 HIGH (DevOps): "policy without mechanism
   110	is hope." The RC hold (originally a 7-day calendar gate per ADR-014;
   111	reduced to a 24h Codex re-pass window per ADR-103) is now enforced by a
   112	step in `release.yml` that:
   113	
   114	1. Skips check on RC tags (`v*-rc.*`).
   115	2. On GA tags (`v1.x.y`), finds the most recent `v1.x.y-rc.*` tag via
   116	   `git tag -l --sort=-creatordate`.
   117	3. If no prior RC → fail (mandatory RC before GA).
   118	4. Else compute delta; reject if <24h (86400s).
   119	
   120	Step lives in the `release-gate` job between "Assert VERSION matches
   121	tag" and "Assert CHANGELOG entry exists" — fails fast before any
   122	heavier checks run. Uses `creatordate` (unified for lightweight +
   123	annotated tags) and `fetch-depth: 0` (already set on checkout).
