   122	
   123	### Changed — install/upgrade semantics (PLAN-166/167/168)
   124	
   125	Adopter-visible behavior of `scripts/install.sh` / `scripts/upgrade.sh`
   126	changed in this release — what a v1.2.0 adopter notices when upgrading:
   127	
   128	- **Ownership is ONE decision, not a cascade (ADR-190).** Whether the
   129	  framework owns `PROTOCOL.md`, `SPEC/v1` or
   130	  `.claude/.framework-version` is answered by a single pure function
   131	  (`_ownership_verdict()` in `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh`, a
   132	  function of 10 observed dimensions); `install.sh` and `upgrade.sh`
   133	  observe → call → execute — they no longer decide locally. Contract:
   134	  `docs/ownership-decision-table.md`.
   135	- **`SPEC/v1` is a forced route on upgrade.** A framework-owned
   136	  `SPEC/v1` is backed up to `.claude.bak/<timestamp>/SPEC/v1` and
   137	  replaced wholesale — a local edit is a fork of the published
   138	  compliance contract, not a customization. A pre-existing `SPEC/v1`
   139	  with no delivery record is byte-compared against the pristine SPECs
   140	  shipped at v1.2.0 and earlier: a match refreshes it, anything else is
   141	  preserved in place with a named WARNING (ADR-155-AMEND-1). Skipped on
   142	  `--ceremony user` installs.
   143	- **`.claude/.framework-version` is the authoritative version marker.**
   144	  Written on install and rewritten on every upgrade;
   145	  `check-framework-updates.sh` and forensic triage read it
   146	  MARKER-FIRST. The adopter repo's root `VERSION` file is deliberately
   147	  never touched by upgrade — after upgrading, the marker (not root
   148	  `VERSION`) is what carries the installed framework version.
   149	- **`PROTOCOL.md` pointer has ONE generator.** Install and upgrade
   150	  render the pointer through the same shared generator (byte-identical
   151	  output on both paths); a degraded pointer body is cured with a backup
   152	  and adopter edits are preserved. Skipped on `--ceremony user`
   153	  installs, which never create root files.
   154	
   155	### Governance
   156	
   157	- ADRs 184 → **190** (ADR-185 night-mode; ADR-186 hook-deadline policy;
   158	  ADR-110-AMEND-2; ADR-164-AMEND-1; ADR-155-AMEND-1 delivery-record
   159	  ownership; ADR-190 ownership-decision-table contract). Slash
   160	  commands 26 → **27**
   161	  (`/night-mode`). All four ceremony phases landed as separable
   162	  Owner-GPG-signed commits with per-phase sentinels and closed scopes.
